Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi, one way to deal with this might be to use a binomial offset, say something like:

phi~dunif(0, 1)
...

for (k in (f[i]+1):nyear){

phi_k[k]<-1-(1-phi^difftime[k-1]) ####here difftime is the temporal distance between primary periods in whatever unit you would like survival to correspond to

z[i,k] ~ dbern(mu1[i,k])

    mu1[i,k] <- phi_k[k]* z[i,k-1]

    mu2[i,k] <- p * z[i,k]

....

Another way might be to model survival as a hazard rather than a probability, and use a log-log type link ( see https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.13059).

John

